{"name":"Floating Lily Pad","hex":"#ccc7a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"floating","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["That floats or float.","Not fixed in position, opinion etc.; free to move or drift."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle and gerund of float"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/floating"},{"term":"lily","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several flowers in the genus Lilium of the family Liliaceae, which includes a great many ornamental species.","Any of several species of herbaceous flower which may or may not resemble the genus Lilium in some way, and which are not closely related to it or each other."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["White ."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lily"},{"term":"pad","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Paumarí."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A flattened mass of anything soft, to sit or lie on.","A cushion used as a saddle without a tree or frame."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pad"}],"entries":[{"title":"Nymphaeaceae","blocks":[{"text":"Nymphaeaceae is a family of flowering plants, commonly called water lilies. They live as rhizomatous aquatic herbs in temperate and tropical climates around the world. The family contains five genera with about 70 known species. Water lilies are rooted in soil in bodies of water, with leaves and flowers floating on or rising from the surface. Leaves are oval and heart-shaped in Barclaya. Leaves are round, with a radial notch in Nymphaea and Nuphar, but fully circular in Victoria and Euryale."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/11/Nymphaea_nouchali5.JPG/330px-Nymphaea_nouchali5.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nymphaeaceae"},{"title":"Lilium","blocks":[{"text":"Lilium is a genus of herbaceous flowering plants growing from bulbs, all with large and often prominent flowers. Lilies are a group of flowering plants which are important in culture and literature in much of the world. Most species are native to the Northern Hemisphere and their range is temperate climates and extends into the subtropics. Many other plants have \"lily\" in their common names, but do not belong to the same genus and are therefore not true lilies. True lilies are known to be highly toxic to cats."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Lilium_candidum_1.jpg/330px-Lilium_candidum_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lilium"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg/500px-Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg/500px-Barclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flowering Barclaya longifolia specimen, Thailand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarclaya_longifolia_in_Thailand_crooped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg/330px-Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg/330px-Victoria_cruziana_flower.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Flower of Victoria cruziana, Santa Cruz water lily","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVictoria_cruziana_flower.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg/500px-Euryale_ferox_kz06.jpg?utm_source=e